# Architecture rules

- Distinguish **normative design** (`Architecture/`, `Master of the Sword module/`) from **implementation** (`apps/`, `packages/`, `docs/adr/`, `docs/implementation-status.md`). Report gaps; do not silently rewrite canon to match incomplete code.
- Full school manifest canon: `Master of the Sword module/fencing-school/module-manifest.yaml`. The file under `modules/fencing-school/` is a short stub only.
- Events are immutable facts. Corrections are new events. No in-place history rewrite.
- Single authoritative writer per aggregate; cross-engine changes via typed async protocols and approved read contracts.
- At-least-once delivery + inbox dedup + domain idempotency + transactional outbox (atomic with state). See `Architecture/002a-platform-contract-standard.md` and `docs/runbooks/outbox-stuck.md`.
- Context Modules must not compute primary Level/XP; Engines own progression surfaces declared in RFCs.
- Keep domain logic independent of UI/transport/framework details; prefer explicit contracts at boundaries.
- Avoid circular dependencies and hidden global state; make side effects visible behind adapters.
- For cross-package changes, document compatibility, rollout, and rollback; record decisions in `docs/adr/` when consequential.
- Introduce a new abstraction only when at least two concrete use cases justify it or the boundary is required for testing/security.
